# `@polygonlabs/maticjs` live-read test environment
#
# Copy to `.env.test` and populate. The repo's .gitignore covers that file;
# keep it that way and never commit it: a URL carrying an API key is a secret.
# Every live test is a read, so no private key or wallet is needed. Writes
# run against a local devnet in `packages/e2e` (see its README.md).

# Testnet RPC URLs. With both set, the bridge-token and adapter files under
# `tests/live/` run against Sepolia (parent) and Amoy (child); with either
# unset they skip. Free public endpoints may rate-limit. The parent URL also
# feeds the Sepolia staking reads, which replay a pinned block, so it must
# be archive-capable.
POS_SDK_TEST_PARENT_RPC=
POS_SDK_TEST_CHILD_RPC=

# Optional mainnet RPC URLs. The exit-payload, staking-read and permit-domain
# files always run, against these when set and public defaults otherwise.
# The staking reads replay a pinned block, so these must be archive-capable.
# Leave them commented out rather than empty: an empty value replaces the
# default instead of falling back to it.
# POS_SDK_TEST_MAINNET_PARENT_RPC=
# POS_SDK_TEST_MAINNET_CHILD_RPC=
